id: pm-h06944
title: "Two governance loosenings sit in the committed assurance registry with no entry in the append-only workspace audit stream, which freezes every future audited write and is invisible to both validate and health"
description: ""
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: assurance,ci,governance,history,immutability,integrity
created_at: "2026-08-13T08:59:21.974Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T08:59:53.906Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "The audited workspace stream replays to exactly the on-disk state of every workspace singleton it governs, verified by a check that compares replay against disk rather than only verifying the hash chain; The two divergent assertions are reconciled by a recorded mutation that states which value is intended and why, never by editing either file to match the other; pm validate and pm health both report singleton-replay divergence, so a committed divergence fails CI at the commit that introduces it instead of freezing the next writer; A direct edit to a workspace singleton that bypasses the audited mutation path is refused or reported at the point the change is committed, with a negative control proving detection; The loosening-authorization guard is proven to classify a tightening as a tightening, with a negative control for each bound polarity, so an earned stricter bound never requires the authorization a weaker one does; Assurance registry writes are restorable to any recorded version, demonstrated by restoring the registry to a prior state and replaying forward"
goal: provable-history
objective: "The audited stream for a workspace singleton always reproduces the singleton, and any divergence is reported by an integrity surface before it blocks a write"
value: "The append-only workspace stream is the proof that a governance bound was never weakened silently. Two bounds were weakened silently, so for the assurance registry the proof does not currently hold."
impact: "The assurance registry is unmutatable through its own audited path: every pm assurance put fails with a state conflict, so no bound can be tightened, no gate promoted, and no earned ratchet locked in."
outcome: "The divergence is reconciled by a recorded entry, the two loosenings are either re-authorized or reverted on the record, and an integrity check reports singleton-replay divergence so it can never again be discovered only by attempting a write."
why_now: Discovered by attempting a legitimate tightening this session; the registry has been frozen since 2026-08-13 and neither of the two standing integrity surfaces reports anything wrong.
parent: pm-33cw
risk: critical
confidence: 95
